# Copy to .env.local before running `pnpm dev:live` / `pnpm test-client`.
# This package is fully isolated from apps/broker and every other PayBound
# package/env file — nothing here is read from or written to those.

# --- Server (src/index.ts) ---
PORT=3210

# Hedera testnet facilitator. Testnet by default; do not point this at
# mainnet without re-reading Blocky402's mainnet docs first.
BLOCKY402_URL=https://api.testnet.blocky402.com

# A Hedera testnet account YOU control — payments settle into this account.
# Get one + fund it at https://portal.hedera.com/ (or derive one from an
# existing funded account via AccountCreateTransaction, as this task's
# own setup did).
#
# Day-1 verification reused apps/broker's operator account, 0.0.10421552,
# here — a data-value convenience (it was already funded), not an
# architectural link between this service and the Broker. Give this
# service its own account before that reuse means anything load-bearing.
GATED_PAYTO_ACCOUNT_ID=0.0.xxxxxx

# Price of the gated resource, in tinybars. 100000 tinybars = 0.001 HBAR.
GATED_PRICE_TINYBARS=100000

# --- Test client (scripts/test-client.ts) ---
GATED_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:3210

# A *different* Hedera testnet account (the payer/buyer role) — must be
# funded with testnet HBAR. Get one + fund it at https://portal.hedera.com/.
#
# Day-1 verification created + funded 0.0.10480198 for this role (5 HBAR,
# funded from apps/broker's operator account; ~4.998 HBAR left after two
# 0.001 HBAR settlement runs) — see README.md's "Test accounts" section for
# the account ID; the DER private key lives only in .env.local (gitignored,
# never committed). Reuse it for Day 2's live-demo integration rather than
# creating yet another payer account, unless it runs dry.
PAYER_ACCOUNT_ID=0.0.xxxxxx
# DER-encoded private key, per PrivateKey.fromStringDer.
PAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=302e...
